                        "text": "<system-reminder>\nAs you answer the user's questions, you can use the following context:\n# claudeMd\nCodebase and user instructions are shown below. Be sure to adhere to these instructions. IMPORTANT: These instructions OVERRIDE any default behavior and you MUST follow them exactly as written.\n\nContents of /Users/apple/.claude/projects/-Users-apple-Projects-al-llm-warden/memory/MEMORY.md (user's auto-memory, persists across conversations):\n\n- [Always insert a row for monitored response flows](feedback_response_events.md) — never silently `return` from response() in addon.py; use `_write_skipped` so every tapped flow leaves a row.\n- [SSE parser must cover tool/thinking deltas](project_sse_parser_shapes.md) — Claude Code traffic is mostly tool_use, not text_delta; extractors must pull input_json_delta/thinking_delta or rows go missing.\n- [Proxy ports must bind to 127.0.0.1](project_proxy_port_binding.md) — plain `8080:8080` exposes warden as an open relay; on Mac+WARP, off-host traffic floods it and every site times out + Claude Code SSL errors.\n- [mitmproxy connection_strategy must stay lazy](project_mitmproxy_connection_strategy.md) — eager presents warden CA for passthrough hosts when upstream fails → Chrome SSL warnings on Gmail.\n- [Docker bridge MTU must be 1380 for warden-proxy](project_docker_bridge_mtu.md) — default 1500 hangs container outbound TLS on macOS (vpnkit PMTU black hole); custom network with MTU 1380 in compose is required.\n- [Warden TLS cert untrust confirmed 2026-05-07](project_warden_tls_cert_untrust.md) — Chrome ui_security_indicator URL = host-side CA chain break, not MTU; resume with uninstall→keychain purge→killall trustd→reinstall→warden-trace.sh.\n- [macOS scripts must work on bash 3.2](feedback_macos_bash_compat.md) — no `printf '%(...)T'`, no assoc arrays, no `${var,,}`; macOS ships bash 3.2.57 and won't upgrade.\n# userEmail\nThe user's email address is saumyemalhotra94@gmail.com.\n# currentDa