                    {
                        "content": "1\t---\n2\tname: warden-tls-debug\n3\tdescription: Resume the warden-on-macOS TLS-break debugging session — when warden proxy is enabled, ALL HTTPS through proxy hangs (claude.ai, claude code, anthropic API, gmail, google all timeout 0 bytes). MTU theory disproved 2026-05-08 — TLS handshake completes, request sent, response never arrives. Suspect: mitmproxy upstream forwarding or addon hang. Deep-trace instrumentation laid down. Repo at /Users/apple/Projects/al_llm_warden.\n4\t---\n5\t\n6\t# Warden TLS Debug — Deep-Trace Instrumentation Phase (2026-05-08)\n7\t\n8\t## RESUME PROTOCOL — read THIS FIRST (supersedes older sections below)\n9\t\n10\t### Where we are (as of 2026-05-08)\n11\t\n12\tUser ran `scripts/warden-trace.sh` post-MTU-fix. Initial reading me thought L6a \"PASS\" meant anthropic was reachable — **wrong.** L6a is openssl s_client direct from container (bypasses mitmproxy). User corrected: claude.ai + Claude Code + browser ALL still dead.\n13\t\n14\t**Critical finding from L4a/L4b raw logs (`warden-trace-20260507-201601/`):**\n15\t```\n16\tapi.anthropic.com via proxy:\n17\t  ✓ CONNECT tunnel established (200)\n18\t  ✓ TLS handshake COMPLETE — TLSv1.3 / h2 ALPN / mitmproxy cert verified\n19\t  ✓ HTTP/2 GET /v1/models — \"Request completely sent off\"\n20\t  ✘ 12s timeout — 0 bytes received\n21\t```\n22\t\n23\t**This nukes the MTU/PMTU theory.** Handshake clean = path MTU is fine for cert flight. The break is **after request, before response** — i.e. mitmproxy upstream forwarding side OR addon hook hang.\n24\t\n25\t### New prime suspects",
