                        "id": "toolu_01CUaQj8C4oxyHGJpnXx2dRf",
                        "input": {
                            "file_path": "/Users/apple/.claude/skills/warden-tls-debug/SKILL.md",
                            "new_string": "---\nname: warden-tls-debug\ndescription: Resume the warden-on-macOS TLS-break debugging session. ROOT CAUSE FOUND 2026-05-08 evening — half-installed state: system proxy enabled but mitmproxy CA missing from keychain → host rejects every TLS handshake. Fix = clean uninstall+reinstall. MTU/addon/upstream theories all disproved. Repo at /Users/apple/Projects/al_llm_warden.\n---\n\n# Warden TLS Debug — Resolved (2026-05-08 evening)\n\n## ROOT CAUSE — read THIS FIRST (supersedes everything below)\n\nAfter 2 days of misdirected debugging, deep-trace nailed it. Symptom (ALL HTTPS via proxy hangs/timeouts) is **not** MTU, **not** addon hang, **not** upstream forwarding. It is:\n\n> **System proxy is enabled and pointing at warden, but the mitmproxy CA is not in the host keychain.** Every HTTPS request is routed to mitmproxy, which presents its own CA, which the host has no reason to trust → TLS handshake aborted by client → curl/Chrome see timeout/hang.\n\nThis is a half-installed state — typically caused by uninstall (or partial install) wiping the keychain entry while leaving `networksetup` proxy config in place.\n\n### Diagnostic signature (from `warden-deep-trace-20260508-150529/`)\n\n1. **Mitmproxy itself reports it directly.** In `/data/warden-deep-trace.jsonl`:\n   ```\n   \"ev\": \"tls_failed_client\",\n   \"err\": \"The client disconnected during the handshake. If this happens\n           consistently for api.anthropic.com, this may indicate that the\n           client does not trust the proxy's certificate.\"\n   ```\n2. **Event histogram** (`jq -r .ev /data/warden-deep-trace.jsonl | sort | uniq -c`):\n   ```\n    493 client_connected         ← clients keep arriving\n    484 http_connect             ← CONNECT tunnel established\n    458 server_connected         ← upstream reachable\n     33 tls_start_client          ← TLS attempted\n     23 tls_failed_client         ← ~70% of those rejected by client\n     10 tls_established_client\n   ```\n   `server_connected ≫ tls_established_client` → upstream is fine, the break is on the client→mitmproxy hop.\n3. **Trust check confirms missing CA:**\n   ```bash\n   security find-certificate -a -c mitmproxy /Library/Keychains/System.keychain\n   security find-certificate -a -c mitmproxy ~/Library/Keychains/login.keychain-db\n   # Both return: nothing.\n   ls ~/.config/warden/   # Missing too.\n   ```\n4. **System proxy still active:**\n   ```\n   HTTPSProxy : 127.0.0.1\n   HTTPSPort  : 8080\n   HTTPSEnable: 1\n   ```\n\nIf you see this combination — **no CA in keychain + proxy still configured** — stop debugging and run the fix below.\n\n### Fix protocol\n\n```bash\nbash /Users/apple/Projects/al_llm_warden/scripts/uninstall-mac.sh\nsudo killall trustd\nsleep 3\nbash /Users/apple/Projects/al_llm_warden/scripts/install-mac.sh\n# At the install prompt for closing browsers, say YES.\n```\n\nIn a **fresh terminal** verify all three:\n```bash\necho $HTTPS_PROXY    # http://127.0.0.1:8080\nls ~/.config/warden/ # warden-ca-bundle.pem must exist\nsecurity find-certificate -c mitmproxy -p /Library/Keychains/System.keychain \\\n  | openssl x509 -noout -fingerprint -sha256\n# must match: 98:61:93:60:01:A6:30:71:08:01:28:20:90:C9:30:2A:58:B7:20:98:F3:81:1C:20:F6:DB:64:AA:25:AD:04:DD\n```\n\nThen Chrome **full quit (Cmd+Q) → reopen** → load `https://claude.ai`. If it loads clean, run `curl -v https://api.anthropic.com/v1/models` and start Claude Code.\n\n### Theories ruled out — DO NOT re-investigate\n\n| Theory | Status | How disproved |\n|---|---|---|\n| MTU/PMTU black hole | ❌ wrong | Container `openssl s_client` to mail.google.com handshake completes cleanly while host probes hang. Unrelated. |\n| Addon hook deadlock (LSTM/SQLite blocking event loop) | ❌ wrong | Failures are at `tls_failed_client` — mitmproxy never reaches `requestheaders`, so no addon hook ever fired. |\n| mitmproxy upstream HTTP/2 forwarding broken | ❌ wrong | `server_connected: 458` proves upstream is reachable. The few flows that complete TLS handshake also complete responses (e.g. `update.googleapis.com 200`). |\n| SSE stream tap deadlock | ❌ wrong | Same reason — never reach the response phase. |\n| Stale/duplicate CA in keychain | ❌ not this case | Keychain is **empty**, not duplicated. |\n| trustd cache stale (Apple Secure Transport) | ❌ wrong | Trust isn't stale — it's literally absent. |\n\n### What about the deep-trace instrumentation?\n\nThe instrumentation laid down on 2026-05-08 (`backend/proxy/debug_addon.py`, `WARDEN_DEEP_TRACE=1` plumbing in entrypoint/Dockerfile/compose, `scripts/warden-deep-trace.sh`) **earned its keep** — it surfaced the `tls_failed_client` event with the verbatim mitmproxy hint. Keep it. For future re-debugging, the run protocol is unchanged:\n\n```bash\nsudo bash /Users/apple/Projects/al_llm_warden/scripts/warden-deep-trace.sh\n# Output: warden-deep-trace-<ts>/\n```\n\nAlways read in this order:\n1. `state/scutil_proxy.txt` — is system proxy on?\n2. `security find-certificate -c mitmproxy ...` on host — is CA in keychain?\n3. **If those two disagree (proxy on but CA missing), stop. It's the trust-gap bug. Re-run install.**\n4. Only if both look correct, dig into `deep-trace.jsonl` event histogram.\n\n### Memory updates needed (do these on E2E confirmation)\n\n- New: `project_warden_tls_trustgap.md` — symptom + diagnostic signature + fix. The half-installed state is the failure mode that ate two days; memorialize it so we never re-chase MTU/addon ghosts again.\n- Update `project_warden_tls_cert_untrust.md` (2026-05-07) — append: confirmed root cause was trust-gap, not stale-CA. MTU 1380→1280 change in compose is unrelated cosmetic.\n\n---",
                            "old_string": "---\nname: warden-tls-debug\ndescription: Resume the warden-on-macOS TLS-break debugging session — when warden proxy is enabled, ALL HTTPS through proxy hangs (claude.ai, claude code, anthropic API, gmail, google all timeout 0 bytes). MTU theory disproved 2026-05-08 — TLS handshake completes, request sent, response never arrives. Suspect: mitmproxy upstream forwarding or addon hang. Deep-trace instrumentation laid down. Repo at /Users/apple/Projects/al_llm_warden.\n---\n\n# Warden TLS Debug — Deep-Trace Instrumentation Phase (2026-05-08)\n\n## RESUME PROTOCOL — read THIS FIRST (supersedes older sections below)\n\n### Where we are (as of 2026-05-08)\n\nUser ran `scripts/warden-trace.sh` post-MTU-fix. Initial reading me thought L6a \"PASS\" meant anthropic was reachable — **wrong.** L6a is openssl s_client direct from container (bypasses mitmproxy). User corrected: claude.ai + Claude Code + browser ALL still dead.\n\n**Critical finding from L4a/L4b raw logs (`warden-trace-20260507-201601/`):**\n```\napi.anthropic.com via proxy:\n  ✓ CONNECT tunnel established (200)\n  ✓ TLS handshake COMPLETE — TLSv1.3 / h2 ALPN / mitmproxy cert verified\n  ✓ HTTP/2 GET /v1/models — \"Request completely sent off\"\n  ✘ 12s timeout — 0 bytes received\n```\n\n**This nukes the MTU/PMTU theory.** Handshake clean = path MTU is fine for cert flight. The break is **after request, before response** — i.e. mitmproxy upstream forwarding side OR addon hook hang.\n\n### New prime suspects\n\n1. **Addon hook deadlock** — `responseheaders`/`response`/`requestheaders` in `backend/proxy/addon.py` doing synchronous CPU work (LSTM classifier, EventStore SQLite) blocking asyncio event loop\n2. **mitmproxy upstream HTTP/2 forwarding broken** — request never reaches upstream\n3. **SSE stream tap deadlock** — `WARDEN_TAP_STREAMS=1` (default) hooks every chunk; if buffer fills wrong it hangs the flow\n4. **Connection pool exhaustion** — L8 showed flood of `server connect → server disconnect` in 1ms for ssl.gstatic.com (Chrome preconnect storm)\n\n### What's been laid down (2026-05-08, ready for reinstall)\n\n5 file changes for full-stack instrumentation, gated on `WARDEN_DEEP_TRACE=1`:\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `backend/proxy/debug_addon.py` (NEW) | Hooks every TLS event, server_connect/connected/disconnected, requestheaders, responseheaders, error → JSONL at `/data/warden-deep-trace.jsonl` |\n| `backend/Dockerfile` | Adds `tcpdump iproute2 procps lsof dnsutils` |\n| `backend/entrypoint.sh` | When `WARDEN_DEEP_TRACE=1`: starts background tcpdump on eth0 (rotated 5×50MB), loads debug_addon.py as 2nd `-s`, bumps mitmdump `termlog_verbosity=debug flow_detail=4`, runs 5s socket/FD snapshotter |\n| `docker-compose.yml` | Adds `WARDEN_DEEP_TRACE` env passthrough + `NET_RAW`/`NET_ADMIN` caps for tcpdump |\n| `scripts/warden-deep-trace.sh` (NEW) | Host-side mega-trace: sudo tcpdump on lo0 + active interface, parallel probes (anthropic+claude.ai+chatgpt+google+linkedin+plain HTTP), pulls all container artifacts, generates correlation summary |\n\n### Run protocol after reinstall\n\n```bash\n# Reinstall path:\nbash scripts/uninstall-mac.sh\nbash scripts/install-mac.sh\n# Then in fresh terminal:\nsudo bash scripts/warden-deep-trace.sh\n```\n\nOutput bundle: `warden-deep-trace-<ts>/` containing:\n- `SUMMARY.txt` — read first; probe outcomes + event-type histogram + TLS failures + addon errors + socket peaks\n- `deep-trace.jsonl` — every TLS/HTTP/connection event from debug_addon (jq-filterable by `cid`)\n- `host_lo0.pcap` — proxy traffic on host loopback\n- `host_<en>.pcap` — actual egress\n- `container_*.pcap` — container-side capture (rotated)\n- `mitmdump.log` — verbose mitmdump output\n- `sockets.log` — periodic ss/FD counts (catches pool exhaustion)\n- `probes/*.log` — per-probe curl -v with full timing breakdown\n- `state/*.txt` — host network state snapshot\n\n### Reading the JSONL — what to look for\n\nFor a failing flow (e.g. anthropic timeout), find the `cid` and trace its events:\n```bash\njq -c 'select(.peer | contains(\"anthropic\"))' deep-trace.jsonl\n# Should see, in order:\n#   server_connect_attempt → server_connected → tls_start_server →\n#   tls_established_server → requestheaders → responseheaders → flow_error\n# If gap is between requestheaders and responseheaders → upstream stall\n# If gap is at server_connect_attempt → no upstream connect\n# If responseheaders fires but flow_error follows → addon hook hung after read\n```\n\n### If addon hook hang is confirmed\n\nQuick diagnostic toggle to confirm addon is the culprit:\n```bash\n# Disable response monitoring in compose env, restart proxy\nWARDEN_MONITOR_RESPONSES=0 WARDEN_TAP_STREAMS=0 docker compose up -d warden-proxy\n# Re-run a single probe\ncurl -v -x http://127.0.0.1:8080 https://api.anthropic.com/v1/models\n```\nIf response now arrives → confirmed addon-side. Then bisect: re-enable one flag at a time.\n\n### If upstream forwarding broken at mitmproxy level\n\nTry mitmproxy-only (no warden addon):\n```bash\ndocker exec warden-proxy mitmdump --listen-host 0.0.0.0 --listen-port 8081 \\\n  --set block_global=false --ssl-insecure\n# From host, point curl at 8081 instead of 8080:\ncurl -v -x http://127.0.0.1:8081 https://api.anthropic.com/v1/models\n```\n(Need to also publish 8081 on the host side — easier path: `docker compose run` ad-hoc.)\n\n### Memory updates pending\n\n- `project_docker_bridge_mtu.md` — needs nuance: MTU 1380 fixed *container-direct* TLS handshake but is NOT the cure for user-visible failure. Real cause is upstream-side mitmproxy/addon, MTU is necessary-but-not-sufficient.\n- New memory after deep-trace: capture whatever the JSONL reveals as actual root cause.\n\n---",
