                    {
                        "text": "Base directory for this skill: /Users/apple/.claude/skills/warden-tls-debug\n\n# Warden TLS Debug — Deep-Trace Instrumentation Phase (2026-05-08)\n\n## RESUME PROTOCOL — read THIS FIRST (supersedes older sections below)\n\n### Where we are (as of 2026-05-08)\n\nUser ran `scripts/warden-trace.sh` post-MTU-fix. Initial reading me thought L6a \"PASS\" meant anthropic was reachable — **wrong.** L6a is openssl s_client direct from container (bypasses mitmproxy). User corrected: claude.ai + Claude Code + browser ALL still dead.\n\n**Critical finding from L4a/L4b raw logs (`warden-trace-20260507-201601/`):**\n```\napi.anthropic.com via proxy:\n  ✓ CONNECT tunnel established (200)\n  ✓ TLS handshake COMPLETE — TLSv1.3 / h2 ALPN / mitmproxy cert verified\n  ✓ HTTP/2 GET /v1/models — \"Request completely sent off\"\n  ✘ 12s timeout — 0 bytes received\n```\n\n**This nukes the MTU/PMTU theory.** Handshake clean = path MTU is fine for cert flight. The break is **after request, before response** — i.e. mitmproxy upstream forwarding side OR addon hook hang.\n\n### New prime suspects\n\n1. **Addon hook deadlock** — `responseheaders`/`response`/`requestheaders` in `backend/proxy/addon.py` doing synchronous CPU work (LSTM classifier, EventStore SQLite) blocking asyncio event loop\n2. **mitmproxy upstream HTTP/2 forwarding broken** — request never reaches upstream\n3. **SSE stream tap deadlock** — `WARDEN_TAP_STREAMS=1` (default) hooks every chunk; if buffer fills wrong it hangs the flow\n4. **Connection pool exhaustion** — L8 showed flood of `server connect → server disconnect` in 1ms for ssl.gstatic.com (Chrome preconnect storm)\n\n### What's been laid down (2026-05-08, ready for reinstall)\n\n5 file changes for full-stack instrumentation, gated on `WARDEN_DEEP_TRACE=1`:\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `backend/proxy/debug_addon.py` (NEW) | Hooks every TLS event, server_connect/connected/disconnected, requestheaders, responseheaders, error → JSONL at `/data/warden-deep-trace.jsonl` |\n| `backend/Dockerfile` | Adds `tcpdump iproute2 procps lsof dnsutils` |\n| `backend/entrypoint.sh` | When `WARDEN_DEEP_TRACE=1`: starts background tcpdump on eth0 (rotated 5×50MB), loads debug_addon.py as 2nd `-s`, bumps mitmdump `termlog_verbosity=debug flow_detail=4`, runs 5s socket/FD snapshotter |\n| `docker-compose.yml` | Adds `WARDEN_DEEP_TRACE` env passthrough + `NET_RAW`/`NET_ADMIN` caps for tcpdump |\n| `scripts/warden-deep-trace.sh` (NEW) | Host-side mega-trace: sudo tcpdump on lo0 + active interface, parallel probes (anthropic+claude.ai+chatgpt+google+linkedin+plain HTTP), pulls all container artifacts, generates correlation summary |\n\n### Run protocol after reinstall\n\n```bash\n# Reinstall path:\nbash scripts/uninstall-mac.sh\nbash scripts/install-mac.sh\n# Then in fresh terminal:\nsudo bash scripts/warden-deep-trace.sh\n```\n\nOutput bundle: `warden-deep-trace-<ts>/` containing:\n- `SUMMARY.txt` — read first; probe outcomes + event-type histogram + TLS failures + addon errors + socket peaks\n- `deep-trace.jsonl` — every TLS/HTTP/connection event from debug_addon (jq-filterable by `cid`)\n- `host_lo0.pcap` — proxy traffic on host loopback\n- `host_<en>.pcap` — actual egress\n- `container_*.pcap` — container-side capture (rotated)\n- `mitmdump.log` — verbose mitmdump output\n- `sockets.log` — periodic ss/FD counts (catches pool exhaustion)\n- `probes/*.log` — per-probe curl -v with full timing breakdown\n- `state/*.txt` — host network state snapshot\n\n### Reading the JSONL — what to look for\n\nFor a failing flow (e.g. anthropic timeout), find the `cid` and trace its events:\n```bash\njq -c 'select(.peer | contains(\"anthropic\"))' deep-trace.jsonl\n# Should see, in order:\n#   server_connect_attempt → server_connected → tls_start_server →\n#   tls_established_server → requestheaders → responseheaders → flow_error\n# If gap is between requestheaders and responseheaders → upstream stall\n# If gap is at server_connect_attempt → no upstream connect\n# If responseheaders fires but flow_error follows → addon hook hung after read\n```\n\n### If addon hook hang is confirmed\n\nQuick diagnostic toggle to confirm addon is the culprit:\n```bash\n# Disable response monitoring in compose env, restart proxy\nWARDEN_MONITOR_RESPONSES=0 WARDEN_TAP_STREAMS=0 docker compose up -d warden-proxy\n# Re-run a single probe\ncurl -v -x http://127.0.0.1:8080 https://api.anthropic.com/v1/models\n```\nIf response now arrives → confirmed addon-side. Then bisect: re-enable one flag at a time.\n\n### If upstream forwarding broken at mitmproxy level\n\nTry mitmproxy-only (no warden addon):\n```bash\ndocker exec warden-proxy mitmdump --listen-host 0.0.0.0 --listen-port 8081 \\\n  --set block_global=false --ssl-insecure\n# From host, point curl at 8081 instead of 8080:\ncurl -v -x http://127.0.0.1:8081 https://api.anthropic.com/v1/models\n```\n(Need to also publish 8081 on the host side — easier path: `docker compose run` ad-hoc.)\n\n### Memory updates pending\n\n- `project_docker_bridge_mtu.md` — needs nuance: MTU 1380 fixed *container-direct* TLS handshake but is NOT the cure for user-visible failure. Real cause is upstream-side mitmproxy/addon, MTU is necessary-but-not-sufficient.\n- New memory after deep-trace: capture whatever the JSONL reveals as actual root cause.\n\n---\n\n# Warden TLS Debug — Host-Chain-Break Phase (HISTORICAL — 2026-05-07)\n\n## RESUME PROTOCOL — older entry (kept for context)\n\nIf internet dies and we lose context, here's where we are:\n\n1. **MTU 1380 fix is in `docker-compose.yml`** (warden-net section). Container TLS handshake to upstream confirmed working. DO NOT touch this.\n\n2. **New trace script written: `scripts/warden-trace.sh`** — layer-by-layer L0..L8 probe. Run AFTER `install-mac.sh` in a fresh terminal (env vars need to load). Outputs `warden-trace-<timestamp>/SUMMARY.txt` with PASS/FAIL per layer + root-cause hint.\n\n3. **Last symptom on 2026-05-07 (post-MTU-fix):** User ran install-mac.sh, ALL browser HTTPS broke. Initially user said \"Telegram works, Google/Gmail don't\" → this was a red herring; **Telegram desktop bypasses macOS system proxy** (uses its own in-app proxy config). LinkedIn ALSO broke confirming it's a complete browser/system-proxy chain break, not vendor-specific HSTS/QUIC issue.\n\n4. **User's working hypothesis:** stale cert cache somewhere — old mitmproxy CA from previous install lingering in keychain alongside new CA, breaking trust evaluation. The trace script's L3pre layer counts unique mitmproxy CA fingerprints across ALL keychains specifically to detect this.\n\n5. **Next action when resumed:** ask user to run `bash scripts/warden-trace.sh` (after install) and paste SUMMARY.txt. Parse the FAIL layers. Root-cause hint at bottom of SUMMARY tells the next move.\n\n## Why context loss is a real risk\n\nClaude Code itself depends on the warden proxy + cert chain. When install-mac.sh is run and the chain is broken (current scenario), Claude Code can't reach api.anthropic.com anymore. User can run uninstall-mac.sh to restore, but until then this assistant is dead. So save state before user runs install.\n\n## Trace script layer map (memorize)\n\n| Layer | Tests |\n|-------|-------|\n| L0 | Containers up + MTU 1380 inherited |\n| L1 | networksetup + scutil + shell env all point at warden |\n| L2 | TCP 127.0.0.1:8080 + plain HTTP forward |\n| L3pre | **Multi-keychain mitmproxy CA scan — unique fingerprint count** |\n| L3 | Disk vs keychain vs container fingerprint match + verify-cert -p ssl |\n| L4 | MITM host TLS via proxy: without --cacert (system trust) AND with --cacert |\n| L5 | Passthrough host TLS via proxy: must show real Google issuer |\n| L6 | Container → upstream raw (MTU sanity) |\n| L6.5 | Vendor differential — same probe to LinkedIn/Google/Anthropic/Cloudflare |\n| L6.6 | UDP/443 reachability (QUIC bypass risk) |\n| L7 | Direct env-stripped probe (host network sanity) |\n| L8 | mitmdump live log slice during probes |\n\nRoot-cause hints baked into the script at bottom — read SUMMARY.txt's last block.\n\n## If L3pre shows multiple CAs\n\nMost likely scenario based on symptoms. Fix:\n```bash\nbash scripts/uninstall-mac.sh\n# verify all CAs purged:\nsecurity find-certificate -a -c mitmproxy /Library/Keychains/System.keychain\nsecurity find-certificate -a -c mitmproxy ~/Library/Keychains/login.keychain-db\nsudo killall trustd\nsleep 3\nbash scripts/install-mac.sh\n```\n\n## If L4a fails but L4b passes (system trust says no, --cacert says yes)\n\ntrustd cache stale. Apple Secure Transport ignoring fresh keychain entry.\n```bash\nsudo killall trustd\nsleep 3\n# Quit + relaunch Chrome/Safari\n# Retry trace\n```\n\n## If L5 fails (passthrough hosts broken)\n\nMeans CONNECT tunneling itself broken. Probably MTU still wrong (1380 not actually inherited — L0d will reveal) or allow_hosts regex too greedy and trying to MITM Google. Last resort: drop bridge MTU to 1280:\n```yaml\n# docker-compose.yml warden-net section\ncom.docker.network.driver.mtu: 1280\n```\nThen `docker compose down && docker compose up -d`.\n\n## If L6 fails (container → upstream broken)\n\nMTU fix didn't actually apply. Check:\n```bash\ndocker exec warden-proxy ip link show eth0 | grep mtu\n```\nShould show `mtu 1380`. If still 1500, the network wasn't recreated — `docker compose down && docker compose up -d --force-recreate`.\n\n# Warden TLS Debug — In-Progress (E2E Pending)\n\nUser ko frustrated honest answer chahiye, **terse Hinglish** me jaisa woh khud baat karta hai (`bhai`, `chal`, `bc`). No fluff, no token waste, no defensive language.\n\n## Status (as of 2026-05-07)\n\n🟢 **Container-side TLS handshake fixed.** `docker-compose.yml` me custom bridge network with MTU 1380 added. Confirmed via:\n```\ndocker exec warden-proxy sh -c 'echo | timeout 8 openssl s_client -connect mail.google.com:443 -servername mail.google.com -brief 2>&1 | head -10'\n```\nOutput: `CONNECTION ESTABLISHED / TLSv1.3 / CN=mail.google.com / Verification: OK`. Pehle `Connecting to <ip>` pe hang ho rahi thi.\n\n🟡 **End-to-end browser test PENDING.** Tab tak mark resolved NAHI karna jab tak:\n1. `bash scripts/install-mac.sh` se system proxy enable + CA trust added\n2. Chrome khol ke Gmail load ho — clean, no SSL warning, no timeout\n3. claude.ai / chatgpt.com bhi load ho — MITM hosts proper trust ke saath\n4. Claude Code (terminal) chale bina TLS error ke\n\nMemory pointer: `~/.claude/projects/-Users-apple-Projects-al-llm-warden/memory/project_docker_bridge_mtu.md` — MTU fix saved as permanent project rule.\n\n## Confirmed (skip karo, dobara test mat karo)\n\n✅ **MTU was the culprit** — Docker bridge default 1500 vs vpnkit clamping caused TLS hang. Fixed with `com.docker.network.driver.mtu: 1380` in custom network `warden-net`.\n\n✅ **mitmproxy CA in System.keychain**, fingerprint `98:61:93:60:01:A6:30:71:08:01:28:20:90:C9:30:2A:58:B7:20:98:F3:81:1C:20:F6:DB:64:AA:25:AD:04:DD` — matches container's serving cert.\n\n✅ **Trust set** via `add-trusted-cert -d -r trustRoot -p ssl -p basic`. Install script architecturally correct.\n\n✅ **allow_hosts regex LLM-only** (api.anthropic.com, claude.ai, chatgpt.com, openai, gemini, etc.). Gmail/Google passthrough by design.\n\n✅ **`connection_strategy=lazy`** in `backend/entrypoint.sh:70`.\n\n✅ **Ports `127.0.0.1:8080`** binding correct.\n\n✅ **No Cloudflare WARP** on user's machine.\n\n✅ **iCloud Private Relay NOT active** — user not signed into iCloud. NSP cache in `defaults` was vestigial only, not routing traffic.\n\n## Resume karne ka flow\n\nRestart ke baad jab user `/warden-tls-debug` invoke kare:\n\n### Step 1: Confirm current state pehle\n\n```bash\nls -la ~/.config/warden/ 2>&1\ndocker ps --filter name=warden 2>&1\ngrep -A3 \"warden-net:\" /Users/apple/Projects/al_llm_warden/docker-compose.yml\n```\n\nYeh batayega: install hua hai ya nahi, containers chal rahe hain ya nahi, MTU fix abhi bhi compose me hai ya kisi ne revert kar diya.\n\n### Step 2: User se pucho — kahan tak pohcha?\n\nThree possibilities:\n- **A) Compose update tak ka kaam ho gaya, install nahi chalaya abhi** → Step 3 ka install run karwao\n- **B) Install chala liya, browser test karna hai** → Step 4 ke E2E checks karwao\n- **C) Browser me kuch tut raha hai** → Step 5 ke E2E debugging me jao\n\n### Step 3: Install (agar nahi chalaya)\n\n```bash\ncd /Users/apple/Projects/al_llm_warden && bash scripts/install-mac.sh\n```\n\nBrowser quit prompt pe **YES** bolne ko keh — warna Chrome new trust nahi padhega. Install ke baad new terminal me check kar `echo $HTTPS_PROXY` — `http://127.0.0.1:8080` aana chahiye.\n\n### Step 4: E2E browser checks (yahin pe conclude hoga)\n\nUser ko bolna in order:\n\n1. **Chrome (full quit Cmd+Q + reopen)** — purani trust state nahi rehni chahiye\n2. Open `https://mail.google.com` — load hota hai? Smooth? **Passthrough host test.** Real Google cert (issuer GTS) dikhna chahiye, mitmproxy nahi.\n3. Open `https://claude.ai` — load hota hai? **MITM host test.** Mitmproxy cert dikhna chahiye, NO \"Not Secure\" warning.\n4. Open `https://chatgpt.com` — same MITM check.\n5. Terminal me `claude` (Claude Code CLI) chala — kaam karta hai bina TLS error ke?\n\nSab pass → **case closed.** Memory me note kar do `project_docker_bridge_mtu.md` me ki E2E confirmed.\n\nAgar koi step fail → Step 5.\n\n### Step 5: E2E debugging (agar browser/CLI me abhi bhi tut raha)\n\nSymptom-based branching:\n\n- **Gmail \"Not Secure\" warning** → Chrome ne nayi trust nahi padhi. `sudo killall trustd` + Chrome full quit + reopen. Agar fir bhi → trustd Admin.plist corruption check karo: `sudo security trust-settings-export -d /tmp/trust.plist; plutil -p /tmp/trust.plist | grep -i mitm`.\n\n- **claude.ai \"Not Secure\"** → mitmproxy CA trust system me galat hai. `sudo security find-certificate -c mitmproxy -p /Library/Keychains/System.keychain | openssl x509 -noout -fingerprint -sha256` chala — should match `98:61:93:60:...:04:DD`. Mismatch → uninstall + reinstall.\n\n- **Sites timeout/hang** → MTU 1380 ne bhi nahi solve kiya, OR compose properly applied nahi hua. Container me dobara `openssl s_client` test chala (Step 1 ka command from memory). Hang hota hai → MTU drop to 1280 try karo (`docker-compose.yml` me bridge MTU `1280` set kar). Phir bhi hang → **Step 6: Bare-metal mitmdump.**\n\n- **Claude Code TLS errors** → `cat ~/.zshrc | grep -A5 warden` — env vars present? `NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS=/Users/apple/.config/warden/warden-ca-bundle.pem`? File exists? Agar file gone → reinstall. New terminal launch karke Claude Code retry kar (env reload ke liye).\n\n### Step 6: Bare-metal mitmdump (last fallback)\n\nAgar MTU 1380 + 1280 dono fail → vpnkit chokepoint hai aur Docker hi galat approach hai. Bare-metal:\n\n```bash\npip install mitmproxy\ndocker compose stop warden-proxy\n# Allow-hosts regex same as backend/entrypoint.sh:39-46 wala\nmitmdump --listen-host 127.0.0.1 --listen-port 8080 \\\n  --set connection_strategy=lazy \\\n  --set stream_large_bodies=5m \\\n  --set \"allow_hosts=$ALLOW_HOSTS_REGEX\" \\\n  -s /Users/apple/Projects/al_llm_warden/proxy/addon.py \\\n  --ssl-insecure\n```\n\nTest agar chal pada → `project_docker_bridge_mtu.md` update karo: vpnkit fundamentally broken, recommend bare-metal as long-term path.\n\n## Files of interest\n\n- `/Users/apple/Projects/al_llm_warden/warden-diag.txt` — last full diag (1261 lines)\n- `/Users/apple/Projects/al_llm_warden/warden-diag-raw/` — raw probe logs\n- `/Users/apple/Projects/al_llm_warden/scripts/warden-diag.sh` — diag script\n- `/Users/apple/Projects/al_llm_warden/scripts/install-mac.sh` — install (cert + env vars + networksetup)\n- `/Users/apple/Projects/al_llm_warden/scripts/uninstall-mac.sh`\n- `/Users/apple/Projects/al_llm_warden/docker-compose.yml` — has the MTU fix (warden-net section)\n- `/Users/apple/Projects/al_llm_warden/backend/entrypoint.sh` — mitmdump cmd + allow-hosts regex\n\n## What NOT to do\n\n- ❌ Pehle se confirmed cheezein dobara verify mat karo (cert trust, port binding, allow_hosts list, connection_strategy, MTU choice itself)\n- ❌ Lambi explanations mat do — terse Hinglish chahiye\n- ❌ Politely / pure English me mat shift karo\n- ❌ \"Trust\" / browser cert rabbit hole me wapas mat ja — woh ruled out hai\n- ❌ Multiple steps ek saath mat batao — sequential, ek-ek confirm karte huye\n- ❌ Tab tak \"fix complete / case closed\" mat bolo jab tak Chrome+Gmail+claude.ai+ChatGPT+Claude-Code sab clean nahi\n- ❌ Naya diag dump mat generate karo unless user maange — fresh signal lagega tabhi\n\n## On final E2E success\n\nJab user confirm kare ki sab clean chal raha:\n\n1. **Update** `~/.claude/projects/-Users-apple-Projects-al-llm-warden/memory/project_docker_bridge_mtu.md` ke end me ek line: \"E2E confirmed YYYY-MM-DD: Chrome+Gmail+claude.ai+chatgpt.com+Claude-Code all working with MTU 1380 fix.\"\n\n2. **This skill ko optionally delete kar sakte ho** (`rm -rf ~/.claude/skills/warden-tls-debug/`) — case closed, future debugging ke liye memory pointers aur diag artifacts hi sufficient.",
